==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
Via {{bor|en|la|-}}, from {{der|en|grc|πρόσθεσις||addition}}, from {{m|grc|προστίθημι||I add}}, from {{m|grc|πρός||towards}} + {{m|grc|τίθημι||I place}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*próti}}, {{m|ine-pro|*préti}} + {{m|ine-pro|*dʰédʰeh₁-||to be putting, to be placing}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|prostheses}}

# {{lb|en|medicine}} An artificial [[replacement]] for a body part, either internal or external.
# {{lb|en|linguistics|prosody}} [[prothesis|Prothesis]].
[[Category:en:Amputation]]

